{"n": 732, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "732.webp", "text": "DESCRIPTION OF ELECTRONIC ABSORBER CONTROL (EDC)\n\nThree different shock absorber settings (comfort, normal and sport) can be selected with a switch in\nthe middle console, The shock absorber selection is indicated with control lamps in the ihstrument\ncluster, An additional contro! lamp (absorber symboi) indicates faults in the electrical system.\n\nThe system monitor control lamp goes out about 1.5 seconds after turning on the ignition. Fault\nreports can be cancelled after elimination of the cause by turning the ignition off and on.\n\nShock absorber settings (bump and rebound stages) are controlled by solenoids on the double-pipe\n92s pressure shock absorbers. The control unit monitors the same setting of all shock absorbers. In\ncase of a fault in the electrical system there is automatic switchover to sport for safety’s sake [all\nsolenoids are without current). There is also switchover to sport, if a speedometer signal is missing\n(car stopped; Vo limit, time delay approx. 1.5 sec.). The system switches back to the selected shock\nabsorber setting as soon as there is a signal again (moving off) within approximately 0.05 seconds,\n\nThere is speed-dependent regulation in the comfort position, There is automatic switchover from\ncomfort to normal setting at a road speed of about 110 km/h (68 mph). It switches back to comfort\nwhen the road speed drops below about 100 km/h (62 mph).\n\nAutomatic switchovers are not displayed by the contro! lamps, since the control lamps only show the\nPosition of the selector switch,", "words": [["DESCRIPTION", 0.266, 0.0849, 0.3414, 0.0968], ["OF", 0.3445, 0.0855, 0.3592, 0.0975], ["ELECTRONIC", 0.3637, 0.0855, 0.4347, 0.0975], ["ABSORBER", 0.4382, 0.0855, 0.4985, 0.0975], ["CONTROL", 0.502, 0.0862, 0.5572, 0.0975], ["(EDC)", 0.5613, 0.0855, 0.5912, 0.0981], ["Three", 0.266, 0.134, 0.2938, 0.1452], ["different", 0.2969, 0.134, 0.3394, 0.1459], ["shock", 0.3425, 0.1346,